    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81311.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "You know, I've only seen it once because I just can't bear to watch it again to see literally a person diving for you eyes because of the compression on their neck. And nobody else saying, what are you doing? Stop intervening in any possible way. And I think it's just seared into our minds and doesn't just make us think about George Floyd but about all those who have been victimized by abusive practices, and that's why there is so much frustration, so much fear in this country that here we are centuries into the dialogue over ending racism, and it seems so reliably well as an institutional force, and we just have to do so much more to take it on.",
