    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's the question we're all struggling with. One of the issues that's being taken up is one in where our our cameras on the police officers required to provide more evidence? How are those files managed? Are there certain choke hold practices that are absolutely banned across the country? Is there a requirement for a clear set of intervening steps before one in the police department uses more aggressive force? And how do we fund training for that across this country? There is a chart that is called eight can't wait and it lays out eight things like betting chokeholds or strangleholds required de-escalation require warning before shooting exhaust opportunities before shooting these kinds of things so There are many ideas by experts that have actually been utilized in a number of police departments around the country. We are now trying to focus congressional attention and have members of Congress be in dialogue with their police departments, be in dialogue with their African-American leaders and other leaders of communities of color, bring these issues forward and say, well, how do we create good practices that will result in taking on and ending discrimination or abusive practices when they occur.",
