    "turn_text": "You know, we are marking the anniversary of Tiananmen Square. And I see these photos and I go, where? is this, surely not America, of officers who have been stripped of their markings, so they do not have a name, they do not have a number, they do not identify what service they serve with, apparently to prevent those branches from experiencing criticism. And it's a dispiriting site, and it goes back to the president's sense of what he believes in is force against protest, not embracing the freedom of speech and freedom of assembly that is at the heart of a republic where citizens have a responsibility to cry out against injustice. And that's what citizens are doing.",
