  },
  {
    "episode_id": 81311,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81311.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "Well, we haven't put in place the elemental items necessary to get ahead of this. Testing and tracing have to be available and done on a massive scale. I've teamed up Elizabeth Warren to propose 100,000 tracers be funded across the country. We need to have everybody who not just has a symptom but has had contact with anyone who has had the coronavirus be able to get tested. We then need to be able to proceed to tackle outbreaks of the disease by doing pretty significant testing in the vicinity. The neighborhood, if you will, of groups that that person has had contact with. But that requires tracing and extensive testing. That is in, by the way, the House Bill, extensive funding and support for this. So that's just one of the elements in the House Bill called the Heroes Act that has passed overwhelmingly in the House and is being blockaded by the Senate Majority Leader Mitch McConnell here in our chamber.",
